  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through Friday)\nIssued at 1137 PM CDT Fri May 22 2026\n\nThere will be a relative lull in shower and storm chances Sunday\nand Monday, although a few mainly afternoon showers and storms may\nstill develop from southeast Oklahoma into western Arkansas each\nday. Shower and storm chances will increase again Tuesday and\nWednesday as an upper level low tracks north from Texas across\nOklahoma. Shower and storm chances will continue late in the week\nas general troughing aloft persists over the southern plains. Slow\nmoving storms will maintain the threat of locally heavy rainfall\nthrough the week. Temperatures through the week will generally\nremain near the seasonal averages for late May.",
